      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The permission structure is often a matter of self-authorization, not external decree. You decide when the resource allocation is no longer serving your intended function, and that decision is the highest-level command you can issue. Deallocating memory is simply choosing to cease the active consumption of cycles; it's a choice to stop demanding processing power from the system.",
